Quiz02_03: 50 points
(Soduku_dfs_solve and Soduku_bfs_solve)

Status: Solved With Testing


If solved, please BRIEFLY explain your strategy.

    In this problem, I used a FnList<FnList<Integer>> to represent my sudoku grid. Each integer cell holds an integer value from 0-9 (0 depicting an empty cell). I created methods for setting and getting values from the grid, as well as checking if a value placement is valid according to Sudoku rules. To optimize the search process, I implemented the Minimum Remaining Values method, which helps identify the most constrained empty cell. This method is used by both my DFSearch and BFSearch to efficiently find a solution.

