Quiz02_05:
30 points plus up to 20 bonus points
(isRBT and genRedBlackBST)

Status: Solved With Testing


If solved, please BRIEFLY explain your strategy.

    I had the isRBT method use a private helper method, checkRBT, to aid it in determining whether or not a certain binary tree was a Red-Black Tree or not. The genRedBlackBST method also ensures that the tree is built with minimal black height by recursively balancing the tree. This optimizes the RBT.


    ***ADDED WITH FIX***

    Because the tree is perfectly balanced and alternates colors on each level, it uses the minimum number of black nodes allowed while still satisfying all red-black constraints. Any attempt to reduce the black height further would force either a red root or a red–red parent/child violation, so this construction achieves the minimal possible black height for any valid RBT with 1,000,000 keys.

