Quiz02_06: 50 points
(reroot and insert on DBST)

Status: Solved With Testing


If solved, please BRIEFLY explain your strategy.

    I first ensured the insert method correctly adds a new key to the tree by performing a binary search and placing the new node as a leaf, while also updating the sizes of nodes up the tree. The reroot method was made to randomly select a node and use rotations (left or right) to make it the root, maintaining the binary search tree properties.
    
